    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a gauntlet today against Cease, whose sub-3.00 xERA profile mandates a cautious approach to our daily efficiency goals. Given the scarcity of our target metric, we are forced into a defensive posture, prioritizing volume over high-ceiling aggression. **Andy Pages** (43.41) edges out **Drake Baldwin** (40.51) as the stronger play today; while both suffer from the significant skill penalty of the opposing pitcher, **Andy Pages** maintains a higher base projection and benefits from a slightly more favorable order positioning at #8 compared to the bottom-of-the-order drain on **Drake Baldwin**. Both hitters find themselves in the \"Marginal\" bucket, essentially functioning as placeholders to maintain our daily game cap efficiency while navigating a matchup that minimizes offensive output.\n\nThe decision to limit the starting lineup to just two active bats was necessitated by the current roster status. With core studs like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** all sidelined due to league-wide scheduling off-days, our offensive depth is severely restricted. Furthermore, the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.** to injury removes our most potent stolen base threat, leaving us without an elite weapon to manipulate the SB category today. Consequently, **Drake Baldwin** was the last man standing in our selection process; his inclusion over other bench options like **Nasim Nunez** or **Cole Carrigg** comes down to his superior xwOBA metrics, though he remains a risky start against a pitcher of this caliber. We are effectively punting today's counting stats to prioritize the preservation of game caps for more favorable series, hoping the tandem of **Andy Pages** and **Drake Baldwin** can scrape together enough production to keep our weekly averages stable.",
